<meta type=article title="Frame border looks">
</meta>

<section | Border looks>

A frameable's border look is selected with `border=<name>`: the document names
the look, and the theme defines how it renders. The starter menu is `accent`,
`thick`, `dashed`, and `subtle`; a named look implies the border is on.

<frame border=accent | An accent-bordered callout.>

<frame border=thick | A thick-bordered callout.>

<frame border=dashed | A dashed-bordered callout.>

<frame border=subtle | A subtle-bordered callout.>

<frame | A plain frame — default border, no named look.>

<aside border=accent | A named look works on any frameable border surface, not just on a frame.>
